## Contract checks beyond the tests

Accepted receipts are the binding contract (both `accepted`):
  preflight-1: desk/reviews/task-queue-run-deja-en-espera-un-trabajo-de-dispatch-start-que-responde-ocupado-en-vez-de-marcarlo-fallid/preflight-1.md
  bundle-1:    desk/reviews/task-queue-run-deja-en-espera-un-trabajo-de-dispatch-start-que-responde-ocupado-en-vez-de-marcarlo-fallid/bundle-1.md
  `deskops review status <task> --root .`: preflight accepted 73602ef13a6d, bundle accepted 2639218029f2 (review-status.txt).

The accepted coordinator resolution says:
  "Un trabajo cuyo código de salida está en retry_exit_codes de su tipo vuelve de
   running a pending (conserva id y nombre, y suma el contador attempts en el JSON),
   queue run imprime 'en espera: <id> ocupado (exit <n>)' y retorna 0 sin correr los
   siguientes, para no saltarse el orden."

Observed implementation (manual-contract-probe.log, /tmp/queue-retry-probe-*):
  - job with retry_exit_codes [3] and command `exit 3` -> back to pending, exit 0,
    no failed job, no inbox note: matches the core requirement.
  - stdout: "en espera: 20261119T131025Z-start-task-probe ocupado"
    MISSING the accepted "(exit 3)" suffix.
  - pending JSON: id/kind/task_id/transition/enqueued_at only.
    MISSING the accepted `attempts` counter.
  - repeated run (manual-contract-probe2.log, no --all, two retries):
    still pending, exit 0, but `attempts` remains ABSENT.
  - `tests/test_queue.py::test_retry_exit_code_leaves_job_pending` only asserts
    "en espera:" + "ocupado", pending/failed/running folders and no inbox note; it
    does not cover the accepted `attempts` counter or the `(exit <n>)` message.

## Verdict

FALLA. The two new tests and the whole test_queue file pass, and the literal task
Goal (pending instead of failed, no unclear note, other exit codes fail) is met.
However the accepted preflight/bundle contract adds two observable requirements that
the executor did not implement and the new tests do not cover:
  1. `attempts` counter in the pending job JSON;
  2. `en espera: <id> ocupado (exit <n>)` including the exit code.
No source, test or desk files were modified by this tester; no commit was created.
